From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:05:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 088/342] block_cache: sub transaction check off

The check of 7b8753c601 ran on the ODROID-C2 for over 120000
cache_start_sub_transaction() calls without finding a block that needed
the walk: fsbench, creating and deleting up to 8000 small files, a 24 MB
RAM disk filled to the last block in three rounds (aborted sub
transactions, checkfs clean), and three power cuts while files were
being created and deleted (the log replayed, no blocks lost or set
twice).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/system/kernel/cache/block_cache.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/system/kernel/cache/block_cache.cpp b/src/system/kernel/cache/block_cache.cpp
index 0a515f3f01..8961c14a10 100644
--- a/src/system/kernel/cache/block_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/system/kernel/cache/block_cache.cpp
@@ -58,7 +58,7 @@
 
 // Checks at every cache_start_sub_transaction() that the blocks it leaves out
 // need nothing done (check_sub_transaction_list()); walks all blocks.
-#define BLOCK_CACHE_DEBUG_SUB_TRANSACTIONS 1
+#define BLOCK_CACHE_DEBUG_SUB_TRANSACTIONS 0
 
 static const bigtime_t kTransactionIdleTime = 2000000LL;
 	// a transaction is considered idle after 2 seconds of inactivity
